<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25581" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lactesco</span></b> , ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i>
			[lacteo]. * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To turn to milk</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis fere cibus matrum lactescere incipit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 51, 128</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 21, 84, § 230
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To have milk for suckling, to become capable of
				giving suck</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asinae praegnantes continuo lactescunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 41, 96, § 237</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug.
					Ep. 150</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">segetes facit lactescere,</span>”
				<i>to become milky</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. G. 1, 315</span></i>
			; v. 2. Lactans.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
